Letting go of competitive sport. Working in a field other than what he studied.
Moving across country, and then across the world. Ended significant relationships.
Changing from individual to manager to individual and back to manager in his career.
Chasing more than a dozen different hobbies (mostly not all simultaneously).

Norm has been through a few changes and reinventions of self, including this work
as a coach.

Where and how can Norm bring a steady presence into your constantly changing life,
to help you find your own center upon which to balance your forward path?






